---
layout: layout.njk
pagination:
  data: datePages
  size: 1
  alias: datePage
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/{{ datePage.days }}-days-from-today/index.html"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ datePage.days }} Days From Today - Exact Date Calculator"
  description: "Find out the exact date that is {{ datePage.days }} days from today. See the day of the week, total weeks, and days remaining."
---

<div class="date-page-container">
    <h1>{{ datePage.days }} Days From Today</h1>
    <p>Need to know the exact date? Below is the calculated calendar date corresponding to exactly {{ datePage.days }} days from today including day of the week detail.</p>

    <div style="background: #eff6ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; text-align: center; margin: 2rem 0; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);">
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #4b5563; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Calculated Future Date</p>
        <div id="out-target-date" style="font-size: 2.6rem; font-weight: 800; color: #1e40af; line-height: 1.2; word-wrap: break-word;">Loading...</div>
        <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;" id="out-countdown">Initializing countdown...</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <div style="background: #f9fafb; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;">
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #6b7280; text-transform: uppercase;">Standard Weeks</div>
            <div style="font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                {{ (datePage.days / 7).toFixed(1) }} weeks
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #f9fafb; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;">
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #6b7280; text-transform: uppercase;">Business Days</div>
            <div style="font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                {{ (datePage.days * 5 / 7).toFixed(0) }} days
            </div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: #9ca3af; margin-top: 0.25rem;">Excludes weekends</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick shift control -->
    <div style="background: #fdf2f8; border: 1px solid #fbcfe8; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #9d174d;">Calculate a custom number of days</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #c21d56; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Change the number of days to instantly see the future date calculated in real time.</p>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
            <input type="number" id="custom-days" value="{{ datePage.days }}" min="1" max="100000" style="flex: 1; min-width: 120px; padding: 0.6rem; border: 1px solid #fbcfe8; border-radius: 6px;" inputmode="numeric">
            <button id="btn-custom-calc" style="background: #db2777; color: #fff; border:none; padding:0.6rem 1.2rem; border-radius:6px; cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Calculate</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="how">
        <h2>How to Calculate {{ datePage.days }} Days From Today</h2>
        <p>To find out what date falls exactly {{ datePage.days }} days in the future, you must add that number of calendar days to today's date. The calculation is simple but requires accounting for the variable lengths of calendar months (28, 30, or 31 days) as well as leap years.</p>
        <p>For example, if you add {{ datePage.days }} days, you are checking a horizon that spans multiple months. Doing this calculation manually is prone to errors, which makes using a dedicated calendar arithmetic tool the safest option.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="formula">
        <h2>Custom Date Arithmetic</h2>
        <p>If you prefer calculating schedule dates manually, divide the total days by 7 to determine the number of weeks involved. Any remaining remainder represents the leftover days to count forward individually.</p>
        <p><strong>{{ datePage.days }} days = {{ (datePage.days / 7) | int }} weeks and {{ datePage.days % 7 }} days</strong></p>
        <p>This layout helps when checking deadlines or billing cycles that must span specific intervals. If you need to add or subtract standard calendar months or years, visit our dedicated <a href="/date-calculator/" style="color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline;">Date Calculator</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <h3>Does this date calculation include weekends?</h3>
        <p>Yes. The future date is calculated by adding calendar days. This includes all Saturdays, Sundays, and public holidays.</p>

        <h3>Does the calculation change during leap years?</h3>
        <p>Yes. The underlying arithmetic accounts for years that contain 366 days instead of 365, ensuring that the target date is completely accurate regardless of the year.</p>

        <h3>Can I schedule payments using this date?</h3>
        <p>Yes, though it is best to verify whether the calculated day falls on a bank holiday or weekend. Financial transactions are typically processed on the next business day.</p>
    </section>

    <section style="background: #f9fafb; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 3rem;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Essential Finance and Wealth Tools</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem; color: #6b7280; line-height: 1.5;">Planning schedule dates is often the first step in financial forecasting. Use our compound interest growth tool to model how investments accumulate wealth over fixed periods, or construct detailed amortization table exports to analyze your debts.</p>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1rem;">
            <a href="/compound-interest-calculator/" style="background: #2563eb; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600;">Compound Interest Calculator</a>
            <a href="/amortization-calculator/" style="background: #4b5563; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600;">Amortization Calculator</a>
            <a href="/date-calculator/" style="background: #10b981; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600;">Full Date Calculator</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

<script>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
        const offset = {{ datePage.days }};
        const outTarget = document.getElementById('out-target-date');
        const outCountdown = document.getElementById('out-countdown');
        const customDaysInput = document.getElementById('custom-days');
        const btnCustomCalc = document.getElementById('btn-custom-calc');

        function updateDate(daysToAdd) {
            const today = new Date();
            const target = new Date();
            target.setDate(today.getDate() + daysToAdd);

            const options = { weekday: 'long', year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' };
            outTarget.textContent = target.toLocaleDateString('en-US', options);

            // Compute countdown
            const timeDiff = target.getTime() - today.getTime();
            const daysRemaining = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(timeDiff / (1000 * 3600 * 24)));
            
            if (daysRemaining === 0) {
                outCountdown.textContent = "The date is today!";
            } else if (daysRemaining === 1) {
                outCountdown.textContent = "Exactly tomorrow";
            } else {
                outCountdown.textContent = "Exactly " + daysRemaining + " days remaining";
            }
        }

        // Initialize with default query offset
        updateDate(offset);

        btnCustomCalc.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const customVal = parseInt(customDaysInput.value) || 0;
            if (customVal > 0) {
                updateDate(customVal);
                // Dynamically update the header for UX clarity (without reloading)
                document.querySelector('.date-page-container h1').textContent = customVal + " Days From Today";
            }
        });
    });
</script>
